    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d443-a1">

                <pb facs="0781" n="711" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg711"/>


                <head>Mr. Washburn to President
                        Lopez</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paso Pucu</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1866-12-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 26, 1866.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am informed that two citizens of the
                    United States, named George’ Wilson and George Bowlin, taken on board the
                    Argentine steamer Veinte Cinco de Mayo, are detained as prisoners in this
                    country. From what I learn of them I think they would be very useful to me as
                    servants, and if your excellency will allow me to employ them as such, without
                    reference to the question of their capture or in any way affecting their
                    position as prisoners, it will be a great favor to me and my family, and will be
                    in harmony with the many other acts of kindness that I have received from your
                    excellency, and entitle you to the profound thanks of your humble and obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES A, WASHBURN.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency Marshal <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lopez, President of
                            Paraguay.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
